<!--
    The framework members CasCore's sandbox admits, rooted for a trimmed desktop build.

    PluginPolicy builds its policy from CasCore's DefaultSandbox, which binds framework members by
    *name* - WithSandboxedSystemConsole resolves Console.get_In, WithSandboxedSystemLinq resolves
    Expression.Lambda, and a group built over an incoming assembly binds by Assembly.Load("...") -
    so the trimmer sees no reference to any of them and drops each one the game's own code never
    uses. Plugin load then fails inside PluginPolicy.Build with "Could not find method get_In to add
    to binding for System.Console" or a FileNotFoundException for the whole assembly.

    A group needs two things, and both are per-assembly here:
      - the assembly *file* present, for the Assembly.Load groups and for forwarders;
      - the type's members kept, for the typeof(...) groups.
    Rooting the assembly does both.

    This is exactly the set DefaultSandbox() enables. Add a group's assemblies when PluginPolicy
    starts using one, and drop an entry when a group goes away. PluginPolicy deliberately skips
    CasCore's JSON group (it throws on this runtime), so System.Text.Json is absent on purpose.

    Desktop only: the sandbox needs dynamic code, so on wasm PluginPolicy.Supported is false and
    plugins load through the plain PluginLoadContext - that head imports PluginTypes.linker.xml
    alone. If wasm sandboxing starts working, import this file there too.
-->
<linker>
    <assembly fullname="System.Private.CoreLib" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Collections" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Collections.Concurrent" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Collections.Immutable" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Collections.NonGeneric" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Collections.Specialized" />
    <assembly fullname="System.ComponentModel.TypeConverter" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Console" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Linq" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Linq.Expressions" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Linq.Parallel" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Linq.Queryable" />
    <assembly fullname="System.ObjectModel" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Reflection.TypeExtensions" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Runtime.Numerics" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Runtime.Serialization.Formatters" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Text.RegularExpressions" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Threading" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Threading.Channels" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Threading.Tasks.Dataflow" />
    <assembly fullname="System.Threading.Tasks.Parallel" />
</linker>
